Context('Numeric');
$v = random(45, 90, 1);
$H = NumberWithUnits($v**2/64 + 6, 'feet');

#############################
# Exercise Group Introduction
#############################

BEGIN_PGML
On Earth, if you throw a baseball straight up at speed [`v`] (in feet per second), the highest that it reaches is [`v^2/64+6`] feet above the ground.

END_PGML

######
# Body
######

BEGIN_PGML
If thrown straight up with speed [`[$v]`] feet per second, how high will the baseball reach?

[_]{$H}{10}

END_PGML

